//    repeatedly perform the single merge with the largest cost saving: detach
//    a whole feeder subtree from the platform and connect one of its turbines
//    to a turbine of another subtree (the detached subtree is re-oriented
//    towards the new connection).  Every merge must respect the 1300 m limit,
//    the 14-turbine capacity of the largest cable along the new path and the
//    no-crossing rule.  Merging continues while it saves money, and then
//    (if more than B feeders remain) with the least costly merges until the
//    feeder-bay limit is met.
